            <ArticleTitle>Psychosocial aspects of hand injuries and diseases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>513-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>More than 50% of patients with a diagnosable psychiatric disorder initially present with somatic symptoms, which often effectively distract the physician from the true illness. Moreover, the occupational setting is ripe for the emergence of psychosocial issues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
